  "title": "Basil II",
  "summary": "Basil II, son of Romanos II, was born around 958 and ruled the Byzantine Empire from 976 until his death in December 1025. His long war with Samuel of Bulgaria included the victory at Kleidion in 1014, and Bulgar lands were incorporated into the empire after he entered Serdica in 1018. He is remembered as the Bulgar-Slayer.",
